  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 318 AM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nWeak mid/upper ridging remains situated across the southern and \ncentral CONUS while a strengthening lee trough over the Central High \nPlains has brought light southerly winds back to the area. This \npattern will linger over the area through a good chunk of the \nupcoming week. The subtle shortwave trough over the Southwest is \nprogged to lift NE toward the Central Plains early in the week which \nwill likely result in an increase in mid lvl clouds on Mon-Tue with \nsome weakening of the mid/upper ridge but dry air in the bottom of \nthe column should preclude light shower activity through the\nwork-week. Temperatures are expected to slowly moderate with \nseasonable values returning to the area on Mon-Tue and above \naverage temperatures anticipated Wed-Sat.\n\nA more robust mid/upper trough will emerge from the Rockies this \nweekend as it shears northeastward into the Northern Plains. This \nmay bring a subtle increase in pops to the area late Sat while near \nor above average temperatures prevail through the end of the \nforecast period.",
